            "pages": {
              "end": 32,
              "start": 32
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Sotomayor, justice Sotomayor questioned whether the mens\u2011rea test takes away the excusing of a person who, historically, would have been considered a lunatic with no volition to fight back."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Alito",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1d40d0ab8170cbb6c4996025f0fa3af3283ebdc9e3052ffa247f1286c63efd94",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1d40d0ab8170-0003-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 67,
              "start": 67
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Alito asked why the petitioner is arguing for a separate insanity defense tied to M\u2019Naghten, noting that historically insanity was linked to mens\u2011rea and applied categorically in every case."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Alito",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1d40d0ab8170cbb6c4996025f0fa3af3283ebdc9e3052ffa247f1286c63efd94",
            "evidence_ids": [
